# The Fedora bootc base every Tilo image builds FROM — mirrored into the
# registry and pinned by digest, exactly like the frozen RPM repo next door in
# os/rpms-snapshot.env.
#
# Why the mirror: Fedora rebuilds the fedora-bootc tag daily and garbage-
# collects the manifest it replaces almost immediately, so a pin straight at
# quay.io stops resolving after about a day ("manifest unknown") and every
# image build dies at its first FROM — including the snapshot-rpms job, so the
# package set can't be refreshed either. Our registry collects nothing, so a
# pin against the mirror keeps resolving while the mirror retains it.
#
# BASE_SOURCE is the upstream tag we track. The `mirror-base` workflow
# (manual dispatch) copies it across with its multi-arch index intact and
# prints the BASE_REF to commit below.
#
# Bumping Fedora major: edit BASE_SOURCE, re-run `mirror-base`, commit the new
# BASE_REF, then re-run `snapshot-rpms` and commit the new RPMS_REF — the
# frozen package set is resolved against this base and has to follow it.
BASE_SOURCE=quay.io/fedora/fedora-bootc:44
# Mirrored 2026-09-20 as ghcr.io/tilo-os/fedora-bootc:44-20260920.
# Copied with --preserve-digests, so this is the same digest and the same bytes
# quay.io served: an OCI index over amd64/arm64/ppc64le/s390x, image version
# 44, ostree.linux 7.2.5-200.fc44.x86_64.
BASE_REF=ghcr.io/tilo-os/fedora-bootc@sha256:6a5d572ec60a704ea10fd3c6deb3b1d557bb1fb04a2f7a8076607ebcdc42ad02
